/bin/
/dist/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/testdata/tmp/
.env

# go build ./cmd/mole without -o drops the binary here
/mole

# Ad-hoc cassettes. The eval corpus (§14.2) will commit its own under a
# deliberate policy; a 1.8MB dump of third-party page HTML recorded during
# development is not that, and git history is hard to undo.
/testdata/cassettes/

# Scratch left by the falsification sweeps: a mutation is applied to a file, the
# suite is run, and the original is restored from a copy. `git add -A` swept two
# of those copies into a commit before this line existed.
*.bak
zz_*_test.go
dist/

# The exhaustive pair labellings. Every pair from two corpus questions judged by
# hand, kept out of the repository on purpose: they are a measurement input, not
# a fixture any test reads, and the labelled sets that DO feed tests
# (contradictions.json, batch-size-arms.json) are tracked beside them.
testdata/pairs/mmlu-exhaustive.json
testdata/pairs/population-exhaustive.json
